(489768, 47523, 4493, '<td valign="top">When photographing someone with a wall behind them you can minimize the hard shadows behind them, by moving them farther away from the wall. The added space allows more room for the shadow to diffuse. You can also try to put something over your flash to help diffuse the light. 5 -danny</td>', 'When photographing someone with a wall behind them you can minimize the hard shadows behind them, by moving them farther away from the wall. The added space allows more room for the shadow to diffuse. You can also try to put something over your flash to help diffuse the light. 5 -danny', '2003-11-19 09:16:06.000000', NULL, 1),
