(490227, 47504, 3032, '<td valign="top">Original comment: "Err, that pose is not what you''d call anti-terrorism, it''s more like "hail that idiot from germany"...<br/>Apart from that, good pic."<br/> <br/>Well, that association with the second world war and germany was right, but up to your message about it I didn''t catch the meaning of this photo/ propaganda. I think you are right about this issue, to many people do things and believe things blindly as long as leaders name it "xxx against terrorism / anti-terrorism measures" etc. The terms are abused and the abusers seem to get away with it. But for how long? At one point one has to ask what is worse, the terrorism or the counter measures that affect the people who it is supposed to protect.<br/>Well, that''s a discussion for the political sites and forums, now that I am writing here again I''d like to say a bit more about the photo too.<br/> <br/>I like it how you filled the frame, it puts the figures and their long stretched arms right in your face. The figures/camera are/is positioned at a good angle, it creates depth and avoids a flat looking image.<br/>The lighting is done really well, just as the b&amp;w toning.<br/>I only wonder if the aperture choice was optimal. At one hand I like this version, where there is a slight blur of the second figure. But on the other hand I wonder how it looks if both were in the field of focus. I can image that the scene would become too hard, too sharp and lose some ''emotion''.<br/> <br/>Good luck.</td>', 'Original comment: "Err, that pose is not what you''d call anti-terrorism, it''s more like "hail that idiot from germany"...Apart from that, good pic." Well, that association with the second world war and germany was right, but up to your message about it I didn''t catch the meaning of this photo/ propaganda. I think you are right about this issue, to many people do things and believe things blindly as long as leaders name it "xxx against terrorism / anti-terrorism measures" etc. The terms are abused and the abusers seem to get away with it. But for how long? At one point one has to ask what is worse, the terrorism or the counter measures that affect the people who it is supposed to protect.Well, that''s a discussion for the political sites and forums, now that I am writing here again I''d like to say a bit more about the photo too. I like it how you filled the frame, it puts the figures and their long stretched arms right in your face. The figures/camera are/is positioned at a good angle, it creates depth and avoids a flat looking image.The lighting is done really well, just as the b&w toning.I only wonder if the aperture choice was optimal. At one hand I like this version, where there is a slight blur of the second figure. But on the other hand I wonder how it looks if both were in the field of focus. I can image that the scene would become too hard, too sharp and lose some ''emotion''. Good luck.', '2003-11-19 17:02:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(490228, 47723, 4493, '<td valign="top">I really, really like the use of light in this shot. Very creative! Overall mood and tone carry well throughout the image. 7 -danny</td>', 'I really, really like the use of light in this shot. Very creative! Overall mood and tone carry well throughout the image. 7 -danny', '2003-11-19 17:02:57.000000', NULL, 1),
